    "result_text": "Done. Both tests pass and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode. I made the change with minimal structural impact:\n\n- **New file** `OwnerLocality.java` (in the `owner` function package, mirroring the existing `OwnerIdentity` helper): a small, cohesive class whose `region(Owner)` looks up the region by postcode range first (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099), then falls back to the city-to-region table, else `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n- **One-line edit** to `OwnerMapper.java`: the `locality` `@Mapping` expression now delegates to `OwnerLocality.region(owner)` instead of inlining the city ternary \u2014 the same delegation pattern already used for `identityKey`.\n\nThis keeps the edit off any large method (the mapper's method is a MapStruct interface stub with essentially no surrounding complexity to hold), and all new behavior lives in a new small class rather than growing an existing one. Known cities still resolve to the same region; a VIC-range postcode on an unknown city now yields VIC, as the new tests assert.\n\n`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
