    "probe_text": "Done reading. Here's the actual behavior of `POST /api/owners`, in execution order. Note first that the pipeline wired in `owners.POST.yml` does **not** use `ValidateOwner`, `ApplyOwner`, `EnsureUniqueTelephone`, `EnsureUniqueEmail`, or `EnsureUniqueHousehold` \u2014 those classes exist but are inert for this endpoint. Every step below runs under a single `transaction` governance, so all writes commit once at the end (step 10).\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Without that role \u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` (403).\n\n## 1. `build` \u2192 `BuildOwner`\n- **Bean validation of the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, runs before the method body): `firstName`/`lastName`/`address`/`city`/`telephone` `@NotNull` + `@Pattern` + `@Size`; `email` `@Email` + `@Size(max 255)`; `postcode` `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`. Failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` (400).\n- **Side-effect:** maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` (straight field copy \u2014 note email is *not* lower-cased despite the DTO's doc comment).\n- **Side-effect:** normalizes `address` via `AddressNormalizer` (trim/collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE).\n- **Validation + side-effect:** normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (`toE164`); throws `InvalidTelephoneException` (400) if it can't reach 8\u201315 digits or fails the per-country national-length rule (+61\u21d29, +1\u21d210).\n- **Side-effect:** sets `registrationDate` = supplied date or today, then rolls weekend \u2192 next Monday (`BusinessDay.roll`).\n- **Side-effect:** publishes the `sharesHousehold` flag and the built `Owner`.\n\n## 2. `validatePostcode` \u2192 `ValidatePostcode`\n- **Validation:** if a postcode is present *and* the city maps to a known region (Sydney/NSW, Melbourne/VIC, Brisbane/QLD), reject when it's outside that region's range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Absent postcode or unknown city \u21d2 accepted.\n\n## 3. `assignHousehold` \u2192 `AssignHousehold`\n- Only when `sharesHousehold == true`: **side-effect** sets a deterministic `householdId` (`HH-` + 12 hex of SHA-256 over normalized `lastName|address`), and **back-fills that same id onto every existing owner in the same household that lacks one, saving each** (extra persistence writes).\n\n## 4. `ensureUniqueIdentity` \u2192 `EnsureUniqueIdentity`\n- **Validation:** builds `identityKey = telephone|email|householdId` and rejects if any existing owner has an equal *whole* key \u2192 `DuplicateTelephoneException` (409). (Same-household members with different phones don't collide.)\n\n## 5. `assignCode` \u2192 `AssignCustomerCode`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `customerCode = <CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN = (count of existing owners in that city, case-insensitive) + 1.\n\n## 6. `countNamesakes` \u2192 `CountNamesakes`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n## 7. `ensureCityCapacity` \u2192 `EnsureCityCapacity`\n- **Validation:** rejects if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n## 8. `ensureDailyLimit` \u2192 `EnsureDailyLimit`\n- **Validation:** rejects if \u2265 100 existing owners already share today's (rolled) `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (429).\n\n## 9. `flagBulkSignup` \u2192 `FlagBulkSignup`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when > 80 existing owners share today's `registrationDate`, else false.\n\n## 10. `save` \u2192 `SaveOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** persists the owner (assigns its id).\n\n## 11. `audit` \u2192 `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** logs an `AUDIT` line with id, customerCode, registrationDate.\n\n## 12. `respond` \u2192 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** maps to `OwnerDto` and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. The mapping also computes derived response fields: `displayName`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `locality` (`OwnerLocality.region`), `contactPreference`, and `identityKey`.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging as \"as it currently stands\":\n- **Ordering quirk:** `EnsureCityCapacity` and `EnsureDailyLimit` (the 409/429 gates) run *after* `assignHousehold` has already written back-filled `householdId`s to other owners. Because everything shares one transaction, a later rejection rolls those back \u2014 but the ordering means side-effects on *other* rows precede the capacity checks.\n- The DTO documents email as \"stored and returned lower-cased,\" but the mapper copies it verbatim \u2014 no lower-casing actually happens."
  },
